###############################################################################
# Q11 -- Computational resources
###############################################################################

# MD timings of the short- and long-range water models on one NVIDIA L40S
# GPU (48 GB) are shown only in Fig. 8: LR models run at roughly half the
# speed of SR models and fit about 10,000 atoms on the GPU (SR about
# 30,000). No per-atom number is given.

###############################################################################
# Q12 -- Gaps and ambiguities (prose; not triples)
###############################################################################

# - Introduces LES and combines it with CACE: 'In the present work, we combine LES with Cartesian atomic cluster expansion (CACE) MLIP' (Introduction). Recorded in the registry as CACE-LES derived from CACE. LES is described as applicable to other MLIPs (HDNNP, GAP, MTP, ACE, NequIP, MACE); only the CACE combination is used here.
# - The NaCl errors are root-mean-square percentage errors (CACE-LR T=0: 1.9% energy, 2.3% force; T=1: 1.4%, 1.8%; Table I), which the metric types of the schema do not cover; they are not encoded.
# - The bulk-water and interface errors appear only as learning curves (Figs. 2, 5, 7); those models have no result. The text says force MAEs of about 14 to 27 meV/A on the interface data at 90% training.
# - For the water models the text says 'no message passing (T = 0) or no message passing layer (T = 1)'; T = 1 is read as one message-passing layer, as in the rest of the paper. The interface models use 'the same settings' as bulk water, so the water settings are repeated there.
# - The dimer molecules are not named beyond their class (charged or polar); energy errors are on binding energies in meV per dimer.
# - The DFT code and numerical settings of the three data sets are not given in this paper; the NaCl data set's level of theory is not stated.
# - Author affiliations are not encoded (ORCIDs are those deposited with the DOI metadata, source: crossref).
# - Evaluation roles and data, base models, inference timings with their system sizes, and the source location of each value are recorded in the encoding input (artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/cheng2025.yaml) until the schema has terms for them.

